h2-tag">1. Encapsulation</h2><p class=3D"sc-edbWYL jDhHuH markdown-p-tag" d=
ata-testid=3D"markdown-p-tag">Encapsulation in Java is a process of wrappin=
g related code and data together into a single unit, for example, a capsule=
 which contains several medicines.</p><img src=3D"https://s3.ap-south-1.ama=
zonaws.com/new-assets.ccbp.in/frontend/content/java/java-rm-encapsulation-c=
apsule-example.jpg" alt=3D"capsule" style=3D"width: 350px;"><p class=3D"sc-=
edbWYL jDhHuH markdown-p-tag" data-testid=3D"markdown-p-tag">In Java, the i=
dea behind&nbsp;encapsulation&nbsp;is to ensure that implementation details=
 are not visible to users by hiding data within a class to prevent unauthor=
ized access and avoid unnecessary modifications from outside the class.</p>=
